# {%.Name%}

A {%.LanguageLabel%} service owned by **{%.Team%}**. Runs on the internal developer platform.

## Deploying

Push a semver tag. CI builds the image, pushes it to ECR, and opens a PR
against [`{%.PlatformRepo%}`](https://github.com/{%.PlatformRepo%}) that bumps
the image tag. When that PR merges, ArgoCD syncs it.

```bash
git tag v0.1.1 && git push origin v0.1.1
```

Untagged pushes to `main` build and scan the image but do not deploy.

## Configuration

Runtime config lives in the platform repo, not here:

{%range .Envs%}- `argocd/applications/{%.%}/values/{%$.Name%}.yaml`
{%end%}
Change resource size, replicas, ingress paths, or env vars by opening a PR
against those files. Everything not set there is inherited from the platform's
`standard-service` chart.

## What you get by default

| | |
|---|---|
| Runtime | {%.LanguageLabel%} |
| Resource profile | `{%.Profile%}` |
| Port | `{%.Port%}` |
| Rollout strategy | `{%.RolloutStrategy%}` |
| Ingress | {%if .Ingress%}`{%.IngressPath%}`{%else%}none (cluster-internal only){%end%} |
| Autoscaling | HPA, 2–10 replicas on 80% CPU/memory |
| Network policy | default-deny, DNS + 443 egress only |
| Pod security | non-root, read-only rootfs, all caps dropped |
| TLS in transit | cluster-wide via Cilium WireGuard |

Replica count is managed by the HPA, not by a field in the values file.

## Required endpoints

The chart's probes expect these to exist:

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/healthz` | liveness — process is alive |
| `/readyz` | readiness — ready to take traffic |
| `/metrics` | Prometheus scrape |

## Container image

The generated `Dockerfile` is a starting point, not a finished build. Check the
`CMD` line points at your real entrypoint before the first tag.

The platform runs every pod non-root with a read-only root filesystem and all
capabilities dropped. Anything your service writes at runtime needs a mounted
volume; writing to the image filesystem fails in the cluster even though it
works under `docker run` locally.

## Repo setup

CI needs these set on this repository:

| Kind | Name | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Variable | `AWS_ROLE_ARN` | the OIDC role CI assumes to push to ECR |
| Variable | `PLATFORM_APP_ID` | GitHub App ID for platform-repo access |
| Secret | `PLATFORM_APP_PRIVATE_KEY` | that App's private key |

The ECR repository `{%.ECRRepository%}` must exist before the first build.
